1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,147
That ship wasn't on the map when the game started,

2
00:00:02,597 --> 00:00:04,798
and nothing in your fact sheet can do that.

3
00:00:05,698 --> 00:00:08,160
So today you open the other file, the script.

4
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:11,593
You'll read it once, from top to bottom,

5
00:00:12,043 --> 00:00:14,288
and then paste three small cards into it.

6
00:00:15,188 --> 00:00:17,325
And you won't write a line of code.

7
00:00:19,125 --> 00:00:20,972
First, a reminder from Lecture 7.

8
00:00:21,872 --> 00:00:24,509
In your fact sheet, a hash is a heading,

9
00:00:24,959 --> 00:00:27,122
and two slashes are a note.

10
00:00:28,022 --> 00:00:30,421
In the script, it's the other way round.

11
00:00:31,321 --> 00:00:32,654
A hash is a note,

12
00:00:33,104 --> 00:00:35,220
and two slashes start a route,

13
00:00:35,670 --> 00:00:38,118
which is a block that runs when something happens.

14
00:00:39,018 --> 00:00:41,816
So a note of your own, in this file, starts with a hash.

15
00:00:43,616 --> 00:00:45,575
You also had three rules for this file:

16
00:00:46,025 --> 00:00:48,434
change only what's between the quote marks,

17
00:00:48,884 --> 00:00:50,492
never touch a quote mark itself,

18
00:00:50,942 --> 00:00:53,577
and leave the commas alone.

19
00:00:54,477 --> 00:00:56,908
Today, you go a little further.

20
00:00:58,108 --> 00:00:59,591
At the top there's a note.

21
00:01:00,491 --> 00:01:02,799
Then a named box, which is empty for now,

22
00:01:03,249 --> 00:01:06,709
and the word shared means every block in the file can see it.

23
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:11,666
Next, a line that reads a crew roster, which is for Class 3.

24
00:01:12,566 --> 00:01:15,493
Then three lines that make your side,

25
00:01:15,943 --> 00:01:17,900
and one for the music.

26
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:21,900
And here, at the left edge, is the map.

27
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:25,902
This is a label, which means a named block,

28
00:01:26,352 --> 00:01:30,644
and everything indented under it runs once, when the game starts.

29
00:01:31,844 --> 00:01:35,673
Line thirty-five reads your whole fact sheet, and fills the box.

30
00:01:36,573 --> 00:01:40,263
After that, each section is handed to the thing that knows what to do with it:

31
00:01:40,713 --> 00:01:43,007
landmarks, quests, and scans.

32
00:01:43,907 --> 00:01:46,872
Now look at the word in quotes: landmarks.

33
00:01:47,772 --> 00:01:50,108
That's the key in your section heading.

34
00:01:51,008 --> 00:01:54,680
Last time, I said it had to be exactly that word,

35
00:01:55,130 --> 00:01:57,059
and this line is why.

36
00:01:58,859 --> 00:02:04,510
The lines for sides, for a cast, for conversations and for ruins

37
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:07,944
do nothing until your file has those sections.

38
00:02:08,844 --> 00:02:11,557
Then comes the station, and then the hulk,

39
00:02:12,007 --> 00:02:15,983
where you added ghost ship to this line yourself, back in Lecture 7.

40
00:02:16,883 --> 00:02:18,931
And the last line is arrow, END,

41
00:02:19,381 --> 00:02:21,013
which says this block is finished.

42
00:02:22,213 --> 00:02:25,599
There are three things to know, and that's all the theory.

43
00:02:26,499 --> 00:02:27,878
The first is the indent:

44
00:02:28,328 --> 00:02:31,877
it's four spaces, and the lines of a block line up.

45
00:02:32,777 --> 00:02:34,569
The second is arrow END:

46
00:02:35,019 --> 00:02:37,566
the block is done, and nothing under it runs.

47
00:02:38,466 --> 00:02:41,848
And the third is these two blocks, which you already know.

48
00:02:42,748 --> 00:02:45,066
Each one ends by saying a name.

49
00:02:45,966 --> 00:02:47,696
This one says ghost ship found,

50
00:02:48,146 --> 00:02:50,930
which is your word, from Lecture 7.

51
00:02:52,730 --> 00:02:55,218
And the step in your fact sheet says,

52
00:02:55,668 --> 00:02:58,284
done when, signal, ghost ship found.

53
00:02:59,184 --> 00:03:02,269
So that step isn't finished by reach.

54
00:03:02,719 --> 00:03:05,249
It's finished by the script, by name.

55
00:03:06,149 --> 00:03:09,125
You'll paste that same line in a few minutes,

56
00:03:09,575 --> 00:03:12,219
and decide for yourself when it's said.

57
00:03:13,419 --> 00:03:15,885
Your mission has a title, from Lecture 3,

58
00:03:16,335 --> 00:03:20,232
but the map inside it is still called AMD Sample.

59
00:03:21,132 --> 00:03:23,671
So change the words between the quotes.

60
00:03:24,571 --> 00:03:27,600
The line under it is the description.

61
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:31,646
It has one quote mark, at the start, and none at the end,

62
00:03:32,096 --> 00:03:33,776
and that's how it's meant to be.

63
00:03:34,676 --> 00:03:36,459
Just keep it on one line.

64
00:03:37,659 --> 00:03:39,941
It's one command, as always.

65
00:03:40,841 --> 00:03:44,762
Look at the last line: one AMD, and one mast.

66
00:03:45,662 --> 00:03:48,146
Lint has been reading the script every time,

67
00:03:48,596 --> 00:03:50,642
it's just never had anything to say.

68
00:03:52,442 --> 00:03:56,300
So now I break it, by taking out one quote mark.

69
00:03:57,200 --> 00:04:02,092
Lint says story dot mast, compile, line twenty-five,

70
00:04:02,542 --> 00:04:03,932
and it can't read that line.

71
00:04:04,832 --> 00:04:06,572
And its last sentence says

72
00:04:07,022 --> 00:04:09,399
nothing in this mission runs until this is fixed.

73
00:04:10,299 --> 00:04:12,055
Here's the game with that file:

74
00:04:12,505 --> 00:04:15,875
a page headed Mast Compiler Errors, and nothing else.

75
00:04:16,775 --> 00:04:18,290
Nothing of mine is running,

76
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:20,102
and that's from one character.

77
00:04:21,002 --> 00:04:25,308
So, run lint after every change to this file.

78
00:04:26,508 --> 00:04:27,834
Now back to the story,

79
00:04:28,284 --> 00:04:30,960
which runs hulk, lifeboat, home.

80
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:34,086
I want a wait before home,

81
00:04:34,536 --> 00:04:36,806
so the lifeboat step now reveals a new one.

82
00:04:37,706 --> 00:04:41,009
And the new step is done when it hears a signal, tug arrived,

83
00:04:41,459 --> 00:04:43,171
which is my own word.

84
00:04:44,071 --> 00:04:47,880
Lint says the tug step waits for the signal tug arrived,

85
00:04:48,330 --> 00:04:50,320
and nothing in the mission sends it.

86
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:53,144
You've seen this warning before,

87
00:04:53,594 --> 00:04:55,969
and it's right, because nothing does yet.

88
00:04:57,169 --> 00:05:00,657
Go to the end of the file,

89
00:05:01,107 --> 00:05:02,780
and it's always the end.

90
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:06,768
First a note, so I know what this is, and then the route.

91
00:05:07,668 --> 00:05:09,712
The game says quest started

92
00:05:10,162 --> 00:05:11,838
every time a hidden step is revealed,

93
00:05:12,288 --> 00:05:14,246
and this block listens for that.

94
00:05:15,146 --> 00:05:18,570
But it runs only if the step is this one, salvage, slash, tug,

95
00:05:19,020 --> 00:05:21,501
which is the address you write after reveal.

96
00:05:23,301 --> 00:05:24,964
Then there's one line,

97
00:05:25,414 --> 00:05:27,674
and you've read this line before,

98
00:05:28,124 --> 00:05:30,443
because it's how the hulk gets on the map.

99
00:05:31,343 --> 00:05:33,431
It says where, and its name,

100
00:05:33,881 --> 00:05:36,047
then its side and its role,

101
00:05:36,497 --> 00:05:38,559
and what it looks like.

102
00:05:39,459 --> 00:05:42,379
Those are the same facts as a landmark.

103
00:05:42,829 --> 00:05:45,340
The difference is when.

104
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:49,527
And then arrow, END.

105
00:05:50,727 --> 00:05:54,082
Card two is the line from line ninety-three,

106
00:05:54,532 --> 00:05:56,680
with my word in it, tug arrived,

107
00:05:57,130 --> 00:05:59,936
and it's lined up with the line above.

108
00:06:00,836 --> 00:06:03,755
Lint is clean, because something sends the signal now.

109
00:06:05,555 --> 00:06:08,796
Card three is a wait, of twenty seconds.

110
00:06:09,696 --> 00:06:14,263
The lines run from the top down,

111
00:06:14,713 --> 00:06:18,852
so it waits, brings the tug in, and finishes the step.

112
00:06:19,752 --> 00:06:22,741
Then my word list gets a new role and a new signal,

113
00:06:23,191 --> 00:06:24,744
and lint is clean.

114
00:06:25,944 --> 00:06:26,939
Here are four mistakes.

115
00:06:27,839 --> 00:06:30,407
The first is one space short, on one line.

116
00:06:30,857 --> 00:06:34,453
Lint tells me: bad indentation, and the line.

117
00:06:35,353 --> 00:06:41,703
The second is a line pasted one line too low, under arrow END.

118
00:06:42,603 --> 00:06:43,981
It's a warning this time,

119
00:06:44,431 --> 00:06:47,158
and it says this line never runs.

120
00:06:48,058 --> 00:06:49,620
It's only a warning,

121
00:06:50,070 --> 00:06:52,965
but it would stop my story.

122
00:06:54,765 --> 00:06:59,013
The third is the card pasted in the middle of the map.

123
00:06:59,913 --> 00:07:01,357
It's the same warning,

124
00:07:01,807 --> 00:07:03,730
but about a line of the template,

125
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:07,154
and the first thing it says is to move that line up.

126
00:07:08,054 --> 00:07:10,481
Don't do that, because that line is fine.

127
00:07:11,381 --> 00:07:13,888
My card cut the map in two,

128
00:07:14,338 --> 00:07:18,177
and the game would start with no station and no hulk.

129
00:07:19,077 --> 00:07:21,702
So move the card, to the end of the file.

130
00:07:23,502 --> 00:07:26,587
The fourth is the address, misspelled.

131
00:07:27,487 --> 00:07:30,235
Lint says clean, and there's no tug, ever.

132
00:07:31,135 --> 00:07:32,734
Nothing can check that word for you.

133
00:07:33,634 --> 00:07:36,070
The page has the list of what lint cannot see.

134
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:38,764
It's short, so read it twice.

135
00:07:39,964 --> 00:07:42,444
Out to the hulk, and on to the lifeboat.

136
00:07:43,344 --> 00:07:46,710
There's the new step, and no tug, so now I wait.

137
00:07:48,510 --> 00:07:51,598
And there she is, the Salvage Tug.

138
00:07:52,498 --> 00:07:54,928
The step is done, and home is revealed.

139
00:07:55,828 --> 00:07:58,518
So it's back to the station, and the win.

140
00:07:59,418 --> 00:08:01,167
And both logs are empty.

141
00:08:02,367 --> 00:08:06,554
So that's three cards: when, finish a step, and wait.

142
00:08:07,454 --> 00:08:09,583
For your turn, paste the first one again,

143
00:08:10,033 --> 00:08:12,667
change started to succeeded,

144
00:08:13,117 --> 00:08:17,266
and make something of your own arrive when a step is finished.

145
00:08:18,166 --> 00:08:21,402
Next time is the capstone: you ship a mission.
